From 6ddaddf9e9b2915b512e79b4f50b400b110e474d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@deeveeyant.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Homelab patches: self-hosted endpoints, remote embedder,
 pluggable vector backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

These have been running in production on CT26 since ~2026-06 but were only ever
present in the working tree. Committing so they survive a rebuild — the Docker
migration (AI-Lab task #80) would otherwise silently discard them.

- adapters/provider_openai.py: accept an optional base_url so the OpenAI adapter
  can target a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint (the AI-Lab LLM proxy at
  10.0.0.219:17890) instead of api.openai.com.

- embed/embedder.py: support a REMOTE OpenAI-compatible embedding API via
  EMBED_API_URL / EMBED_API_MODEL, falling back to the local SentenceTransformer
  when unset. Lets the embedder share the same pooled model as the rest of the
  stack instead of loading its own copy.

- config.py: add vector_backend ("qdrant" | "milvus") and milvus_uri.

- client.py: pass config.llm_base_url through to the OpenAI adapter, and select
  the vector store via a factory instead of hardcoding Qdrant. Imports
  MilvusStore defensively so pymilvus stays optional.

- vector/milvus_store.py: new Milvus backend implementation.

- .gitignore: ignore .env.bak* / .env.*.bak — secret-bearing backups were
  untracked but NOT ignored, so they could have been committed by accident.
